    <name>TET_CH-2_Flueli_Ranft</name>
    <cmt>Switzerland&apos;s patron saint Nikolaus von der Fluehe aka Brother Klaus used to live in his little shack down at the river Grosse Melchaa. After quite a successful military and political career Nikolaus decided to leave his wife and family at the age of 50 and set himself up as a hermit. Soon, he became a widely known spiritual guide and consultant and thanks to his counsel even a swiss civil war has been prevented. His shack is still down at the river and just a 20mins walk away from TET Switzerland.</cmt>
    <desc>Switzerland&apos;s patron saint Nikolaus von der Fluehe aka Brother Klaus used to live in his little shack down at the river Grosse Melchaa. After quite a successful military and political career Nikolaus decided to leave his wife and family at the age of 50 and set himself up as a hermit. Soon, he became a widely known spiritual guide and consultant and thanks to his counsel even a swiss civil war has been prevented. His shack is still down at the river and just a 20mins walk away from TET Switzerland.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>user</type>
  </wpt>
